GIFT=["can call a flame into an open palm","hears the leylines hum under the market","dreams of the Heart every new moon","can close a cut with a touch","frosts the well in high summer","calms dogs and horses with a word","finds water under dry ground","sees grey in the veins of the Blight-touched","can quiet a storm for an hour","lights candles by looking at them","moves a feather without touching it","feels a calamity rise, like a headache, days before the news","can read the last thing a dead person saw","makes bread rise in a cold oven","can't be lost in the dark","hears lies as a ringing in the ears","burns whatever is held too long","knows when a beacon has gone dark","sings and the room falls asleep","sees the leyline from the circle to the beacons"]
SIT=["and hides it from the whole household","and has told only the priest","and is quietly paid by Dame Matilda to report","and wants a place at the tower school","and is terrified of being 'awakened' in public like the cobbler","and sells small charms on market day","and sits in the conclave's inner nine","and is blackmailed by the town thief","and was turned away by the tower school","and is teaching it to a child, in secret","and owes a debt to Margaret the Sage","and has started to hear something answering from the east","and is courted by the Company of the Lantern","and is engaged to a hero who doesn't know","and once used it to kill, and nobody knows"]
QUIET=["Its oldest woman remembers the Stewards riding through, and is the last living witness to the Breaking.","A boundary stone was moved last winter; two families are one insult away from killing each other over it.","The miller cheats everyone, and everyone knows, and nobody can prove it.","A stranger has been lodging here all season and pays in Sunward silver.","Its watchmen sleep on duty because nothing ever happens. One night something will.","It is the birthplace of one of the lord's heroes, who sends coin home and never visits.","Its well was dug by the Stewards, and the stones are carved with a shield before a hearth.","Two of its sons ran off to the outlaws. Their mother leaves bread at the woods' edge every night.","Its priest keeps the parish register, and the births, deaths and marriages in it map every feud in the hold.","It brews the best ale in the hold, and the lord's steward taxes it twice.","An orphan here has an *Arcane spark*, and the village doesn't know whether to hide her or sell her to the tower school.","Its fields are the best in the hold, and the lord's steward wants them for the keep's own demesne.","A widow here was a sellsword once. She still keeps a good sword under the bed.","It is quiet because it pays the nearest outlaw band, quietly.","Its smith is the only one for miles, and every band wants him.","A pedlar comes every week with news. Half of it is invented, and the village believes all of it.","Its church bell was cast from a Steward's shield, and the priest won't ring it for anyone but a king.","A shepherd here found a jar of grey salt in a ditch and is using it to cure meat.","The lord's huntsmen trample its crops every season, and the hamlet hates the lord for it.","A son of the hamlet died in the guild last year. His party says it was a beast. His father thinks it was his party.","It has never been raided, and the other hamlets resent it for that.","Its people are all one family, three generations deep, and they marry in.","Someone has been leaving offerings at the stone on the hill, and the priest wants to know who.","Its headman cannot read, and the steward's clerk exploits that every tithe day.","Its youngsters drift to the town for work, and the old folk are left to work the fields.","A deserter from the Iron Reavers is hiding here as a farmhand.","It is famous for one thing: a hound that killed a wolf alone. The hound is old now.","A wise woman here sends the sick to the hospice rather than the temple, and the priest calls her a witch.","Its people speak an older dialect, and town folk think they're simple. They aren't.","There's a cellar under the chapel full of weapons from the Breaking that nobody remembers storing.","Its harvest festival is the best in the hold, and the lord comes in person, with his enemies.","A girl here is betrothed to a merchant twice her age to pay the family's debts.","The road through it is the shortest route between two towns, and the toll it charges is illegal.","It shelters refugees from a lost hamlet, and the newcomers want land.","Someone has been stealing from the barn, and the village blames the refugees.","Its watchman was a hero's squire once, and was dismissed for something he won't speak of.","Its children play at 'Stewards and Horrors', a game nobody remembers inventing.","The ford by it floods every spring, and every spring someone drowns.","It keeps a stone circle's key, an old iron thing the sorcerers would pay for.","A hermit in the woods above it is either a saint or a murderer, depending on who you ask.","It grows the herbs the Little family pays most for, and the Littles' rivals want the land.","Its woman headman is the only one in the hold, and the steward ignores her letters.","A noble's bastard was fostered here and doesn't know it.","Its folds are guarded by its best archer, a girl of fifteen.","It is a day's walk from a lair, and it is ready to run at the first sound.","The guild party of five stops here for water, and the innkeeper's daughter has fallen for their thief.","Its granary was built by the Stewards and has never burned, though men have tried.","A traveller died here in the spring with a sealed letter nobody dares open.","It sends one son to the lord's garrison every year, and gets one back in a box every other year.","An old stone marks a mass grave from the Breaking, and nobody ploughs that field.","It worships at the wayside shrine instead of the town temple, and pays its tithes to Mother Alice.","Its headman is in the steward's pocket and reports every grumble."]
EVENT={'abandoned':["Abandoned and resettled again and again; the resettlers are strangers to each other, and someone is buying the land cheap each time it empties.","Each time it's abandoned, the same family is first to flee and first to return, and they seem to know when the raids will come.","The resettlers found the last family's food untouched. They left in a hurry, or they never left."],
'overrun':["Blight-born came out of the dark and the people ran. The guild cleared it, but the well still tastes of salt.","Overrun by Blight-born; the survivors swear the pack was led by a figure walking upright.","The Blight came through, and now the hamlet's goats give grey milk."],
'occupied':["Outlaws farmed its fields while its people fled to town. Now they're back, and one family who stayed and fed the outlaws is shunned."],
'slavers':["Families here wait on ransoms from the slavers' holds. Some never come home.","It drove the slavers off once and trains every grown person with a spear now."],
'raid':["Raided so often that the watchmen sleep in the church. They'll pay anyone who stops it, in grain, because they have no coin.","After the raids, a farmer is forging spearheads in secret, and the outlaws have heard.","Raided by the same band twice; the second time the raiders knew where the grain was hidden.","Its people fought back during a raid and won once; now the band wants revenge.","The raiders spared the priest's house each time, and the village wonders why.","Burned once, it rebuilt with stone walls paid for by a debt to Sunward moneylenders.","Its young men joined the band that raided it, because the band was eating and the hamlet wasn't."],
'moves':["Wolves at the folds every night; the shepherds want the lord's huntsmen, and the lord's huntsmen are busy."],
'ambush':["Its grain carts are lost on the road, and the hamlet suspects the escort sold the route."]}
EVENT['slavers']+=["The slavers took the miller's twins. He has sold the mill to pay one ransom and must choose which child.","A girl came home from the holds of the north with a slaver's brand and a slaver's language, and now she translates for the ransomers.","The headman paid the slavers *not* to come, and they came anyway. The hamlet wants its coin back.","Its watchmen were asleep the night the slavers came. One was paid to be.","It sends a man to the hospice every month to ask about ransom money that the Sunward fund keeps 'delaying'.","The slavers left a mark on its gate: a promise to return, or a warning to pay.","Its smith's apprentice was taken, and the smith has gone north alone to buy him back."]
EVENT['ambush']+=["Its carts were lost twice in a week, and the carter who survived both times now has new boots.","It now sends its grain by night on the old Steward causeway, which nobody else remembers.","The escort ran at the ambush; the hamlet wants the sergeant who chose them flogged.","It has stopped sending grain to town at all and is hoarding it, which the steward calls rebellion.","The ambushers left the hamlet's own cart behind with the grain still in it, and took only the sealed letter.","Its farmers now ride with the carts armed with flails, and nearly killed a pilgrim by mistake.","A highwayman who robbed its carts sends some grain back to the poorest families."]
EVENT['abandoned']+=["The last time it emptied, someone stayed: an old man who refuses to leave his wife's grave.","It has been abandoned so often that the town no longer counts its tithe, which suits its smugglers."]
EVENT['overrun']+=["After the Blight-born came, its priest blessed the ground and it held. Now pilgrims come, and Brother William visits.","The pack took its herd and left the people, which nobody can explain."]
EVENT['occupied']+=["The outlaws who held it left the fields better tended than they found them, and some farmers miss them."]
EVENT['slavers']+=["The slavers paid a family here for a 'servant girl' last year, and the hamlet has never forgiven them.","Its people now sleep in the church tower when the moon is dark, the slavers' favoured night.","A slaver came back here as a pilgrim, and the widow who recognised him has told no one yet."]
